{
  "file": "questions",
  "name": "Checkout questions and answers",
  "order": 15.8,
  "description": "Questions an event asks buyers at checkout (\"T-shirt size?\", \"Dietary needs?\", \"Company name\", \"I agree to the venue's photo policy\") and what buyers answered: docs/checkout-questions.md. A question is asked once per order (`scope: order`) or for every ticket (`scope: ticket`; a table ticket type is asked per seat), optionally only for some ticket types (`tier_ids`). Kinds: text, long_text, single_choice, multiple_choice, checkbox, number, date, phone, email. Answers are checked at checkout (required, options, lengths, ranges, one entry per ticket), stored on the order before payment and attached to each ticket as it is issued, with the question's label as it was at purchase (`label`; `current_label` is today's). `value` is the normalised answer (text, a number, true, or a list of options in the options' order) and `display` the same as text, which is DICE's `fanSurveyAnswers { fanSurveyQuestion { title } value }` (title = `label`, value = `display`). Every ticket in GET /v1/events/:id/attendees, GET /v1/orders/:id, GET /v1/tickets and GET /v1/tickets/:id carries its `answers`: its own (per-ticket) answers always, and its order's answers only for a credential with orders:read (the credential's scopes decide, not its user's or creator's role). A key holding only tickets:read, such as a door or check-in integration, gets per-ticket answers only. Deleting a question archives it: it is no longer asked, and its answers stay. Writes need an organization API key created by an owner or manager. POST /v1/events/:id/organizer-reservations/:token/complete takes optional `answers` ({ order, tickets }) for the reservation's tickets, checked the same way but never required.",
  "endpoints": [
    {
      "id": "list-event-questions",
      "method": "GET",
      "path": "/v1/events/:id/questions",
      "summary": "List an event's questions",
      "description": "Every question of the event in order, archived ones last, each with its `answer_count`.",
      "auth": "api_key",
      "scope": "events:read",
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "id",
          "location": "path",
          "type": "string (UUID)",
          "required": true,
          "description": "The event's id. Another organization's answers 404.",
          "example": "3f2a9c10-1c2d-4e3f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b"
        }
      ],
      "responses": [
        {
          "status": 200,
          "description": "OK.",
          "example": {
            "data": [
              {
                "id": "5c1e2d3f-4a5b-4c6d-8e7f-901a2b3c4d5e",
                "event_id": "3f2a9c10-1c2d-4e3f-8a9b-0c1d2e3f4a5b",
                "label": "T-shirt size",
                "help_text": "We print on the night.",
                "kind": "single_choice",
                "options": [
                  "S",
                  "M",
                  "L",
                  "XL"
                ],
                "required": true,
                "scope": "ticket",
                "tier_ids": null,
                "max_length": null,
                "min_choices": null,
                "max_choices": null,
                "min_value": null,
                "max_value": null,
                "sort_order": 0,
                "hidden": false,
